{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MISOAlertStatus"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are two types of statuses:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-functional statuses used for informational or decorative alert messages.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They provide context or highlight content without implying a specific state, system event, or user action.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These alerts are not tied to UX patterns such as success, error, or warning, and may use contextual or brand-related icons to enhance recognition or storytelling.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Functional statuses communicate specific system statuses, results, or user feedback:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each variant conveys a clear semantic meaning and must always be paired with its dedicated functional icon to ensure clarity and accessibility.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use functional alerts to inform user about state changes, confirmations, or issues that are directly connected to system logic or user actions.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These messages carry functional meaning and help guide user response or acknowledgment.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:14MISOComponents15MISOAlertStatusO","modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"title":"MISOAlertStatus","symbolKind":"enum","fragments":